  - family-names: Rathi
    given-names: Megha
    affiliation: "Department of CSE & IT, Jaypee Institute of Information Technology, Noida, India"
    email: megha.rathi@mail.jiit.ac.in
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
# repository-code: "https://github.com/<github-username>/TRIAD-BRCA-plus"
# license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code, figures and tables for TRIAD-BRCA+, a leakage-controlled framework for
  PAM50 breast cancer subtyping on METABRIC with harmonised transfer to
  TCGA-BRCA. It combines a full-panel multi-view representation with eight
  label-free meta-gene modules, a tuned heterogeneous expert triad (RBF-SVM,
  ridge multinomial regression, shallow gradient boosting), an equal-weight
  opinion pool and a balanced-risk decision rule that is Bayes-optimal for
  balanced accuracy.
keywords:
  - breast cancer molecular subtyping
  - PAM50 intrinsic subtypes
  - multi-omics integration
  - heterogeneous ensemble learning
  - Bayes-optimal decision rule
  - data leakage
  - cross-cohort harmonisation
  - METABRIC
  - TCGA-BRCA
